WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.245
Lesson 12.8.

00:00:02.245 --> 00:00:07.760
Institutional-grade custody: MPC, custodians and policy engines.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.728
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:09.728 --> 00:00:11.812
be able to know the custody options

00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:14.301
institutions use, and when they make sense

00:00:14.301 --> 00:00:16.385
for a large personal or family book.

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:18.975
Here's the plan.

00:00:18.975 --> 00:00:20.660
First, the key ideas.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.375
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:24.900
Then, your checklist.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.062
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:31.743
First, Multisig (12.2): several keys, rules

00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:35.577
enforced on-chain, transparent and verifiable.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:39.891
Next, MPC (multi-party computation): one key is split into

00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:44.279
shares held by different devices or parties; signatures are

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:48.162
created together without ever assembling the key.

00:00:48.162 --> 00:00:51.892
The rules are enforced off-chain by the provider's software.

00:00:51.892 --> 00:00:54.278
It works on any chain, but you depend on

00:00:54.278 --> 00:00:57.372
the vendor and can't verify the policy on-chain.

00:00:57.372 --> 00:01:00.413
Then, Qualified custodians: regulated firms

00:01:00.413 --> 00:01:02.717
that hold assets for clients.

00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:06.065
Strong legal protections in some jurisdictions; you

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:09.327
give up self-custody and on-chain flexibility.

00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:13.842
Also, Policy engines: approval workflows (who can approve what,

00:01:13.842 --> 00:01:18.569
above which amount), allowlists, time windows and velocity limits,

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:23.878
available in both institutional MPC platforms and smart-account setups.

00:01:23.878 --> 00:01:27.518
And finally, Hybrid: many large holders use

00:01:27.518 --> 00:01:30.993
a custodian or MPC for long-term reserves

00:01:30.993 --> 00:01:34.633
and multisig/smart accounts for active DeFi.

00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:39.073
Let's look at the diagram: Custody architecture.

00:01:39.073 --> 00:01:40.633
Take a moment with it.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.043
It's everything we've just said, in one picture.

00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:46.858
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:50.796
A $5M family book: cold reserves ($3M) with a

00:01:50.796 --> 00:01:56.703
qualified custodian (legal title, insurance terms read); active DeFi

00:01:56.703 --> 00:02:00.641
($1.5M) in a 2-of-3 multisig with a policy of

00:02:00.641 --> 00:02:05.435
two approvers above $50,000 and an allowlist; hot float

00:02:05.435 --> 00:02:08.903
($20,000) in a limited smart account.

00:02:08.903 --> 00:02:12.288
The succession plan (12.6) covers all three.

00:02:13.588 --> 00:02:15.048
Here's your checklist.

00:02:15.048 --> 00:02:16.583
Do it now, for real.

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.123
First, Custody option chosen per tier, with reasons.

00:02:20.123 --> 00:02:24.758
Next, Vendor/custodian terms, insurance and recovery read.

00:02:24.758 --> 00:02:29.494
And finally, Policy engine rules written: approvers, thresholds, allowlists.

00:02:30.794 --> 00:02:32.004
Question 1.

00:02:32.004 --> 00:02:35.946
MPC vs multisig: where are the rules enforced?

00:02:40.366 --> 00:02:44.641
The answer: MPC: off-chain by the provider's software.

00:02:44.641 --> 00:02:47.076
Multisig: on-chain by the contract.

00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:49.621
Question 2.

00:02:49.621 --> 00:02:51.946
What do you give up with a qualified custodian?

00:02:56.366 --> 00:02:59.556
The answer: Self-custody and on-chain flexibility.

00:03:00.856 --> 00:03:02.126
Question 3.

00:03:02.126 --> 00:03:03.501
What is a policy engine?

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.832
The answer: Rules for approvals, thresholds,

00:03:10.832 --> 00:03:13.291
allowlists and limits on transactions.

00:03:14.591 --> 00:03:15.836
Let's recap.

00:03:15.836 --> 00:03:18.743
Multisig (12.2): several keys, rules

00:03:18.743 --> 00:03:22.656
enforced on-chain, transparent and verifiable.

00:03:22.656 --> 00:03:26.745
MPC (multi-party computation): one key is split into

00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:30.439
shares held by different devices or parties.

00:03:30.439 --> 00:03:35.304
Qualified custodians: regulated firms that hold assets for clients.

00:03:35.304 --> 00:03:37.951
Policy engines: approval workflows (who can

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.718
approve what, above which amount), allowlists.

00:03:42.018 --> 00:03:44.533
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:44.533 --> 00:03:47.888
Next up, Lesson 13.0: Mastery Starter.
